---
import OdeV2Layout from '../../../layouts/OdeV2Layout.astro';
import DataTag from '../../../components/ode-v2/DataTag.astro';
import Status from '../../../components/ode-v2/Status.astro';
import Doors from '../../../components/ode-v2/Doors.astro';
import Finding from '../../../components/ode-v2/Finding.astro';
import { odeMeta, odeRoutes } from '../../../i18n/ode-v2';

const lang = 'en' as const;
const m = odeMeta[lang].home;
const r = odeRoutes[lang];

const doors = [
  {
    who: 'Investors',
    question: 'Is there a defensible position here, and which risks are already on the table?',
    href: r.investitori,
    cta: 'The verdict, in two halves',
    next: 'Then Position: where OdE can compete, and where it cannot.',
  },
  {
    who: 'Research partners',
    question: 'Are these questions real, does the method hold up, and is there a paper in it?',
    href: r.evidenza,
    cta: 'What we still cannot answer',
    next: 'Then the Audit: what we have already checked.',
  },
  {
    who: 'Formulators and buyers',
    question: 'What am I actually buying, and what can I say about it without landing in trouble?',
    href: r.tesi,
    cta: 'The parameter that decides',
    next: 'Then AMSA and Regulation.',
  },
];

const limits = [
  {
    kind: 'contro' as const,
    t: 'There is no clinical evidence on topical tallow',
    d: 'Not one high-grade study of what tallow does to skin when you put it on. That is not a hole in our search. It is the state of the field, and it counts against us as much as anyone.',
  },
  {
    kind: 'contro' as const,
    t: 'Our material changes on the skin, and we do not know which way',
    d: 'Skin bacteria make lipases, and lipases split triglycerides. Petrolatum, mineral oil, squalane and dimethicone give them nothing to work on: those are inert, ours is not. What comes off is a mixture, and its two main components have evidence pointing in opposite directions. Nobody has measured the net effect.',
  },
  {
    kind: 'contro' as const,
    t: 'The market that would pay for the difference is small, and we cannot size it',
    d: 'Where tallow moves in volume, we lose on price. Where qualification is worth paying for, the volumes are tiny and no public dataset breaks them out.',
  },
];
---
<OdeV2Layout title={m.title} description={m.description} lang={lang}>
  <section class="hero">
    <p class="ode-eyebrow hero-eyebrow">
      Twelve databases searched, in six languages
    </p>
    <h1>
      There is no clinical study measuring what tallow does to human skin.
    </h1>
    <p class="hero-lede">
      Not one. Not a weak study, not an old one, not one buried in a language nobody reads. We
      went through twelve databases in six languages before we accepted that, and well before we
      built a company on it.
      <DataTag kind="fonte" label="Internal research: Gap verified across twelve databases: PubMed, EMBASE, Europe PMC, Scopus, Web of Science, Google Scholar, Semantic Scholar, ClinicalTrials.gov, CIR, CosIng, EUR-Lex and the FAO Codex Alimentarius. Targeted searches in Polish, Russian, Chinese, Japanese and Turkish alongside English. Research track 5 v3.0, sections 1.3 and 8." />
    </p>
    <p class="hero-status"><Status kind="lacuna" lang={lang} /></p>

    <div class="thesis">
      <p class="thesis-line">
        If nothing is known and nobody is measuring, the value is not in the tallow.
        <strong>It is in being able to vouch for it.</strong>
      </p>
      <p class="thesis-sub">
        OdE does not sell tallow. It sells certainty about what is inside the drum. In a market
        where nobody measures, whoever measures first writes the standard. We are a laboratory
        first and a producer second.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block" aria-label="Where to start">
    <p class="ode-eyebrow block-eyebrow">Three readers, three different questions</p>
    <Doors doors={doors} />
  </section>

  <section class="block" aria-label="The verification work">
    <p class="ode-eyebrow block-eyebrow">What we checked</p>
    <div class="verif">
      <div class="verif-text">
        <p>
          Before we described a product, we spent months trying to break the idea. What came out
          is an evidence library: every record graded, every source given a persistent
          identifier, every gap logged with the query and the database that produced it. It
          includes an audit of the most cited review in the field, which anyone can repeat in an
          afternoon.
        </p>
        <p class="note">
          No competitor can copy that without doing it again themselves, and it is the only
          reason we think we have earned the right to talk about this material.
        </p>
      </div>
      <a class="verif-cta" href={r.audit}>
        <span class="verif-cta-k">The Audit</span>
        <span class="verif-cta-d">The hole in the evidence, the wrong-material errors in the most cited review, and the claims that would not survive scrutiny.</span>
        <span class="verif-cta-a" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block" aria-label="Limits we state up front">
    <p class="ode-eyebrow block-eyebrow">Three limits, before you find them yourself</p>
    <p class="measure block-intro">
      A risk you own makes everything else more credible. A limit the reader turns up on their
      own destroys the lot. These three are the worst of them, and they are on the home page on
      purpose.
    </p>
    <ul class="limits">
      {limits.map((l) => (
        <li>
          <Finding kind={l.kind} lang={lang} />
          <h2>{l.t}</h2>
          <p>{l.d}</p>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
    <p class="note">
      The whole picture, with nothing softened, is in <a href={r.posizione}>Position</a> and
      <a href={r.investitori}>Investors</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="block block--last" aria-label="What OdE is">
    <p class="ode-eyebrow block-eyebrow">In one line</p>
    <p class="closing">
      A laboratory that qualifies and certifies an ingredient batch by batch, in a category that
      has no standard yet. The tallow is the carrier. The document is the product.
    </p>
  </section>
</OdeV2Layout>

<style>
  .hero { padding: 1rem 0 2.4rem; max-width: 48rem; }
  .hero-eyebrow { margin: 0 0 1.1rem; }
  .hero h1 { font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 5.2vw, 3.3rem); letter-spacing: -0.015em; line-height: 1.08; }
  .hero-lede { font-size: 1.08rem; line-height: 1.62; color: var(--ode-body); margin: 1.3rem 0 0; max-width: 40rem; }
  .hero-status { margin: 1rem 0 0; }

  .thesis {
    margin: 2.2rem 0 0;
    padding: 1.5rem 1.7rem;
    background: var(--green-soft);
    border: 1px solid var(--green-border);
    border-radius: var(--ode-radius);
    max-width: 42rem;
  }
  .thesis-line { font-size: clamp(1.15rem, 2.4vw, 1.45rem); line-height: 1.35; color: var(--ink); margin: 0; font-weight: 300; }
  .thesis-line strong { font-weight: 500; }
  .thesis-sub { font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--body); margin: 0.9rem 0 0; }

  .block { padding: 2.3rem 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--ode-rule); }
  .block--last { padding-bottom: 0.5rem; }
  .block-eyebrow { margin: 0 0 1.2rem; }
  .block-intro { margin: 0 0 1.4rem; font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--body); }

  .verif { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.15fr 0.85fr; gap: 1.8rem; align-items: start; }
  .verif-text p { margin: 0 0 0.8rem; font-size: 0.98rem; line-height: 1.62; color: var(--body); max-width: 34rem; }
  .verif-text .note { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .verif-cta {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr auto;
    grid-template-areas: 'k a' 'd d';
    gap: 0.5rem 0.8rem;
    text-decoration: none;
    background: var(--panel);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: var(--ode-radius);
    padding: 1.3rem 1.4rem;
    transition: border-color 160ms ease, transform 160ms ease;
  }
  .verif-cta:hover { border-color: var(--accent); transform: translateY(-2px); }
  .verif-cta-k { grid-area: k; font-size: 1.3rem; font-weight: 500; color: var(--ink); }
  .verif-cta-a { grid-area: a; color: var(--accent); font-size: 1.1rem; }
  .verif-cta-d { grid-area: d; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.5; color: var(--body); }

  .limits { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(16rem, 1fr)); gap: 1.4rem 1.8rem; }
  .limits h2 { font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 500; color: var(--ink); margin: 0.6rem 0 0.45rem; line-height: 1.35; }
  .limits p { font-size: 0.9rem; line-height: 1.55; color: var(--body); margin: 0; }

  .closing { font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 2.2vw, 1.3rem); line-height: 1.5; font-weight: 300; color: var(--ink); max-width: 40rem; margin: 0; }

  @media (max-width: 780px) { .verif { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 1.3rem; } }
</style>
